// AstrBot Go plugin service contract.
//
// This is the RPC boundary between the AstrBot host process and a plugin
// running as a subprocess (go-plugin, gRPC flavor). Plugin authors do NOT
// touch this file directly; they implement the `sdk.Plugin` struct and call
// `sdk.Serve(&plugin)`. The generated code under ../gen is produced with:
//
//	buf generate
//
// The heavy, platform-specific event/component payloads (message chains,
// metadata) cross the wire as `bytes` of JSON to keep the proto surface small
// and forward-compatible; the SDK (event.go) provides typed helpers.
//
// Bidirectional calls: the HOST serves HostService over the go-plugin gRPC
// broker (fixed AppID 9000). Plugins dial it lazily via the broker to call
// platform actions (OneBot API), send messages, or recall messages. The high
// AppID never collides with go-plugin's auto-incrementing NextId() stream
// (which starts low and is only used when a plugin implementation opts into
// the broker itself).
//
// EventResult is the extension point for handler outcomes: instead of piling
// more ad-hoc bool fields onto every response message, future semantics
// (blocked/consumed/etc.) are added as EventResult fields. Old plugin binaries
// (compiled against a proto without `result`) leave the field unset; hosts
// then fall back to the legacy bool fields (stop/sent/handled) that are kept
// for that exact reason. New plugin binaries fill BOTH the result sub-message
// and the legacy fields so old hosts keep working. Proto3 forward/backward
// compatibility rule: only append fields, never remove/reorder/rename.

